IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-terms`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-amount`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-survivor-allowance`

-- Tests of oa2-part3-survivor-allowance: sections 21 and 21.1. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the
-- words of the section, with the reasoning in the comment. The base case is a survivor born March 15, 1960, asking
-- about September 2022: 62 on August 31, 2022; a survivor since January 2020; 25 years of residence; a citizen; an
-- application made and approved; nothing against payment. Each variant changes only what it names.
-- The month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force is not in the text: July 2000 is a made-up value for the tests.

`test base survivor` MEANS `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month` WITH
    `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` IS TRUE
    `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the person became a survivor` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the person's date of birth` IS YMD 1960 3 15
    `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS 25
    `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS TRUE
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS TRUE
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS TRUE
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS FALSE
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS FALSE
    `the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of the payment period` IS TRUE
    `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS TRUE
    `the spouses or common-law partners made a joint application for an allowance under section 19 before the pensioner's death for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and the payment period is one in respect of which it was made` IS FALSE
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS YMD 2022 9 1
    `the person was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1)` IS FALSE
    `the day on which the person became a survivor` IS YMD 2020 1 10
    `the month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force` IS YMD 2000 7 1
    `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the person left Canada` IS NOTHING
    `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS FALSE
    `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS FALSE
    `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force` IS FALSE
    `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS FALSE
    `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS NOTHING
    `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS NOTHING
    `the month in which the person is released` IS NOTHING
    `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the person dies` IS NOTHING
`test spouse alive survivor` MEANS `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month` WITH
    `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` IS FALSE
    `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the person became a survivor` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the person's date of birth` IS YMD 1960 3 15
    `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS 25
    `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS TRUE
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS TRUE
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS TRUE
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS FALSE
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS FALSE
    `the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of the payment period` IS TRUE
    `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS TRUE
    `the spouses or common-law partners made a joint application for an allowance under section 19 before the pensioner's death for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and the payment period is one in respect of which it was made` IS FALSE
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS YMD 2022 9 1
    `the person was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1)` IS FALSE
    `the day on which the person became a survivor` IS YMD 2020 1 10
    `the month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force` IS YMD 2000 7 1
    `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the person left Canada` IS NOTHING
    `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS FALSE
    `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS FALSE
    `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force` IS FALSE
    `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS FALSE
    `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS NOTHING
    `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS NOTHING
    `the month in which the person is released` IS NOTHING
    `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS FALSE
    `the month in which the person dies` IS NOTHING
