§ `Section 21.1 -- the allowance is not payable after a conviction`

-- (1): informed and satisfied of a conviction in Canada: not payable.
#ASSERT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test conviction`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test no conviction`
-- A conviction by a court outside Canada counts only if the Minister has deemed it to (3).
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test foreign conviction`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test foreign conviction deemed`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(3): the Minister may deem the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(3): the Minister may deem the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` FALSE
-- (8): manslaughter with release on a probation order: the section does not apply. Manslaughter without it, or murder with
-- probation: it does.
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test manslaughter with probation`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test manslaughter without probation`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test probation but murder`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(8): section 21.1 does not apply to the individual` `test manslaughter with probation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(8): section 21.1 does not apply to the individual` `test probation but murder`
-- (2): the conviction reversed, withdrawn or stayed AND all rights of appeal exhausted: payable as if (1) had never applied.
-- With appeals open, (1) still applies.
#ASSERT `s 21.1(2): the individual's entitlement becomes payable as if subsection 21.1(1) had never applied` `test reversed conviction, appeals exhausted`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(2): the individual's entitlement becomes payable as if subsection 21.1(1) had never applied` `test reversed conviction, appeals open`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(2): the individual's entitlement becomes payable as if subsection 21.1(1) had never applied` `test appeals exhausted, conviction stands`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test reversed conviction, appeals exhausted`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test reversed conviction, appeals open`
#ASSERT `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `test appeals exhausted, conviction stands`
-- (2): any amount recovered is repaid when the entitlement is restored.
#ASSERT `s 21.1(2): the Minister must repay any amount recovered from the person` TRUE `test reversed conviction, appeals exhausted`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(2): the Minister must repay any amount recovered from the person` FALSE `test reversed conviction, appeals exhausted`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(2): the Minister must repay any amount recovered from the person` TRUE `test conviction`
-- (4): the person who has received an allowance and is then found convicted: deemed not entitled, debt to recover.
#ASSERT `s 21.1(4): the person is deemed not to have been entitled and the amounts are a debt that the Minister must recover` TRUE `test conviction`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21.1(4): the person is deemed not to have been entitled and the amounts are a debt that the Minister must recover` FALSE `test conviction`
